< {"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":true},"resources":{}},"serverInfo":{"name":"vexdom","version":"0.9.2"},"instructions":"Controls the user’s browser through the Vexdom extension. Tools act on the active tab. Start with page_getPageInfo (or the vexdom://page/diagram resource) to learn what is on the page and get stable selectors, then target elements by selector or visible text. page_screenshot hands the image back to you in the result and writes nothing to disk, so captures you take to see the page for yourself leave no files behind. Pass save: true only when the user asked for a picture they can keep; then read the returned savedTo path back so the image renders, and include that path in your reply. Passwords, keys, tokens and cookies are replaced in every result by a sealed placeholder such as ⟦password:4f2a@example.com⟧; the real value stays in the browser. Pass a placeholder through unchanged as page_fillInput’s value or page_typeText’s text and it becomes the credential at the moment it reaches the field. Anywhere else it is refused, and it is never yours to read, rebuild or repeat. SITE_BLOCKED means the user has put that site off-limits to Vexdom: do not retry it or reach it another way — tell the user.\n\nLess common capabilities each have a guide, opened with vexdom_openSkill: how to go about it, then its tools with their input schemas. Open one when the page calls for it:\n- captcha: get past a “verify you are human” check: reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha, Turnstile (Chromium browsers only)\n- theming: measure the colours and contrast a page paints, and retheme it: dark mode, easier on the eyes\n- diagnostics: read the console errors, exceptions and failed requests behind a page that misbehaves (Chromium browsers only)\n- monitoring: watch a long upload, build or deploy and tell the user when it ends, or come back to something later on a timer\n- downloads: make the page download a file and keep it, and list the files kept so far\n- drag: drag one thing onto another: reorder a list, move a card, pull a slider, draw on a canvas"},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1}
